        ('The answer in 40 words',
         "<div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(76,161,84,0.10),rgba(76,161,84,0.03));border:1px solid rgba(76,161,84,0.35);border-radius:12px;padding:20px 24px;margin:24px 0;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text);\"><strong>The answer:</strong> Blackface darkens the face mask, forehead, and body but leaves wings normal. Blackwing darkens the wing flight feathers to solid black but leaves the face normal. Both are autosomal recessive, non-allelic, and combine to produce Double Black.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:rgba(255,255,255,0.02);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px;margin:16px 0 24px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--text-2);display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;\">\n<span>✓ Last verified: <time datetime=\"2026-07-10\">July 10, 2026</time></span>\n<span>✓ Cross-checked: Martin (2002), MUTAVI, WBO standards</span>\n<span>✓ Zero affiliate links, independent editorial</span>\n</div>"),

